    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), assigned on creation per the formula: **start at 1; +1 for an email; +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`; capped at 3** (level 4 reserved for tenure). The old household-size\u2192GOLD rule is gone, as the new spec doesn't include it.\n\nChanges, each kept in the place it belongs:\n\n1. **`util/MembershipLevel.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-responsibility helper `MembershipLevel.of(Owner)` that owns the level computation. This mirrors the existing `CityRegion` util pattern and is the one source of truth, so the two callers don't duplicate the rule.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the derived response field now targets `membershipLevel` and delegates to the helper (same thin-delegation style as its `locality`/`CityRegion` binding). The old string-tier method and its `MembershipTierEnum` usage are removed.\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=` (via the same helper) instead of tier, per \"anything that recorded the tier \u2026 must record the level instead.\"\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 the `Owner` schema's `membershipTier` (string enum) is replaced by `membershipLevel` (`integer`, min 1 / max 3), which is what regenerates the DTO field/getter and drops `MembershipTierEnum`.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` passes (`$.membershipLevel == 3`), and the audit log line confirms `membershipLevel=3`. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repo.",
